1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Thorgrim "Godi" Þorsteinsson=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chief who lived on the farm Søbol, Haukadal, Isafjorden in Western Norway, Iceland'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Thorgrim was born on the farm Helgafjell, The parents were Thorstein Torskebiter and Thora Olufsdotter
2 CONT * He married Thordis, they had their son Thorgrim, who was called Snorre good
2 CONT * Thorgfim got the farm Sæbol in dowry and he moved there.
2 CONT * He killed Vestein Vesteinsson who was the brother Aud Vesteinsdatter married to his brother-in-law Gisle Sursson (Thorbjørnson.
2 CONT * Thorbjørn was killed on his farm in 963 by Gisle Surrson who revenge the murder of Vestin
2 CONT * Þorgrímur Þorsteinsson Goddad codite Name / Precedence: Thorgrim Location: Vestl. Island Relations: Son of Thorstein Torskebider. Married to Gisle Surson's sister Thordis. Father of Snorre Gode. Sources: Landnamabogen 73, S109, 
2 CONC 110
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.northvegr.org/lore/landnamabok/009.php From "Landnåmabok", Chapter 9:]
2 CONT
2 CONT A daughter of Osvif was Gudrun, the mother of Gellir and Bolli and Florleik and Thord Cat. The son of Bjorn the Easterner was named Vilgeirr. Kjallak the Old married Astrid the daughter of Hrolf, a hersir, and of Ondott, the siste
2 CONC r of Olvir Bairnkarl; their son was Thorgrim the godi, he married Thorhlid, the daughter of Thord the Yeller; their sons were Viga Styrr and Vermand the Slender, and Brand, the father of Thorleik.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%ADsla_saga Brothers Divided Again in Iceland]
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 952,[12] the hero's family leave Norway and move to the Westfjords of Iceland. The siblings marry: Gisli marries Aud, sister of Vestein Vesteinsson; Thorkel marries a woman named Asgerd; and Thordis marries Thorgrim Thorste
2 CONC insson the Godi. They live as neighbors, the brothers at Hol, and Thorgrim at Saebol.[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT While attending a thing (an assembly), the hero's close-knit group learns that a wise man named Gest has predicted discord among them (the "Haukdal men") in three years. To forestall this, Gisli, Thorkel, Thorgrim (brother-in-law 
2 CONC to both), and Vestein (Gisli's brothers-in-law) decide to enter a pact of blood brotherhood (Fóstbræðralag, "foster brotherhood"). However, Thorgrim has a change of heart and the pact is not completed.[14][15] From this moment on 
2 CONC the characters’ actions seem to be largely controlled by fate as they head down a tragic path.[16][17]
2 CONT
2 CONT A chain of dreadful events is set into motion when Thorkel is eavesdropping and overhears his wife Asgerd and Gisli's wife Aud talking about their past loves. Thorkel learns that his wife was actually fond of Vestein before she ma
2 CONC rried. Gisli too learns from his wife that she had been fond of Thorgrim the Godi prior to marriage. Thorkel reacts to the news more badly than Gisli, and first lashes out at his wife by refusing to let her sleep in the same bed a
2 CONC s him, which is immediately quashed by her who threatens him with divorce.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorkel then decides he must part company with his brother, and take up farming with Thorgrim, demanding a division of their assets. Thorkel will relinquish the land and farm, but will claim movable assets, including the broken he
2 CONC irloom sword Grásiða. Thorkel and Thorgrim have the sword reforged as a spear, with the assistance of a black magician and blacksmith named Thorgrim Nef (Nose, or Bottlenose).[19][21]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Vestein's doom=
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorkel now in league with Thorgrim discuss various things, perhaps even planning Vestein's murder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vestein returns from abroad and is reported to be heading for Gisli's home. Gisli sends his farmhands to warn Vestein away, entrusting his messengers with a special coin he crafted as a token of dire danger. But Vestein refuses to
2 CONC  heed the warning. Along the way Vestein meets more people who tell him to be on guard.[22] At Saebol (Thorgrim and Thorkel's farm), the boy Geirmund tells him not to tarry and go straight to Gisli (this boy lived with Gisli and T
2 CONC horkel, until the brothers split their assets). The boy refuses to admit seeing Vestein.[23]
2 CONT
2 CONT While lodging at the home of Gisli and Auda, Vestein is discovered stabbed to death by a spear. The saga states that the custom obligated the person who extracted the murder weapon to carry out vengeance, and Gisli takes the spear
2 CONC  (Grásiða).[a][24] No witness saw the murderer, but Gisli has been haunted by dreams for several nights, and is convinced he knows the murderer.[24] Gisli will later kill Thorgrim, but there are some psychological developments in 
2 CONC the wake of Vestein's death.
2 CONT
