2 CONT Thorkel of Namdalen From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Thorkel of Namdalen was a Norwegian jarl in Namdalen who lived in the mid to late ninth century CE. Thorkel married Hrafnhilda, the daughter of Ketil Trout of Hrafnista. Th
2 CONC eir son, named Ketil Trout after his grandfather, was to become one of the major players in the early settlement of Iceland. Through Ketil Thorolf was the grandfather of Hrafn Haengsson, the first lawspeaker of Iceland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes[edit] Jump up ^ Egil's Saga ch. XXIII.
