1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Two sons: Eirik & Agnar. died when children were young
2 CONT She was the fairest of all women that King Ragnar had heard tell of.
2 CONT
2 CONT The jarl, her father, had given her a baby snake for a present one morning. To
2 CONT begin with, she kept it in a box. But in time, this snake got so big that it
2 CONT coiled right round the bower and bit its own tail. It grew so fierce then that
2 CONT no one dared come near the bower, except her servants and those who fed it,
2 CONT and it ate an ox a day. Folk were very scared, and they could see that it
2 CONT would do great harm, so big and fierce had it become. The jarl made this
2 CONT solemn vow at the bragarfull, the ceremony of the chief's cup, that he would
2 CONT give his daughter Thora in marriage to none but the man who could kill that
2 CONT snake, or who dared go and talk with her there in front of the snake.
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
