1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Auðr the Deep-Eyed Ivarsdóttir (Old Norse: Auðr in djúpúgða) was a Scandinavian princess, the daughter of Ivar Vidfamne, and the mother of Harald Wartooth, who appears in Sögubrot, Hversu Noregr byggdist and in the
2 CONC  Lay of Hyndla. She would have lived sometime during the 7th and 8th centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Ivar Vidfamne Spouses: 1.  Hrœrekr slöngvanbaugi, the king of Zealand 2. Helgi the Sharp 3. king Ráðbarðr of Gardarike
2 CONT
2 CONT LINKS http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Au%C3%B0r_the_Deep-Minded
2 CONT
2 CONT WIKIPEDIA (cont) She was given to a Hrœrekr slöngvanbaugi, the king of Zealand, but would rather have his brother Helgi the Sharp. Ivar Vidfamne solved the problem by telling Hrœrekr that Auðr was unfaithful with Helgi. The ruse w
2 CONC as successful and Hrærekr slew his brother Helgi, after which it was easy for Ivar to attack Hrœrekr and to kill him as well.
2 CONT
2 CONT Auðr fled to Garðaríki with her son Harald Wartooth, and married its king Ráðbarðr with whom she later had the son Randver. Her father king Ivar was upset that his daughter had married without his consent. Although, he was old he 
2 CONC departed to Garðaríki with a large leidang. One night, as they were harboured in the Gulf of Finland, he had a strange dream, and so he asked his foster-father Hörð. His foster-father was standing on a high cliff during the conver
2 CONC sation and told Ivar that the dream foretold the death of Ivar and the end of his evil deeds. Ivar was so angry by these words that he threw himself down into the sea, whereupon also Hörð did the same thing.
2 CONT
2 CONT As the throne of Sweden and Denmark was vacant, Auðr's son Harald Wartooth departed to Scania to claim his inheritance, with the help of his stepfather Ráðbarðr.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Audr Ivarsdottir of_Am (633-) [Pedigree]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Ivar Halfdansson King of Lethra (612-)
2 CONT
2 CONT        REF Halldor Arnason (harnason@u.washington.edu).
2 CONT        Son means son and is never used for daughters. Daughters have
2 CONT        -dottir instead of -son (or -sdottir instead of -sson, the s is
2 CONT        the genitive ending of the father's name). It is however quite
2 CONT        common to see people not familiar with the patronymic system,
2 CONT        mix this up.
2 CONT        The name Audr (the r is a nominative case ending that I like to
2 CONT        keep but most people don't) could both be used as a woman's and
2 CONT        a man's name and maybe there is some confusion because of that.
2 CONT        In later time it became exclusively female.
2 CONT        There is a male Audr in the Norse mythology, but a female one
2 CONT        was one of the settlers of Iceland around 900. She came from
2 CONT        Ireland, so maybe she had an Irish name that sounded somewhat
2 CONT        similar to Audr, so Audr was used for her even though it was
2 CONT        male. I don't know about that, just wondering.
2 CONT        There is a Audr Ivarsdottir mentioned in the poem Hyndluljod as
2 CONT        mother of Haraldr hilditonn Hraereksson and Randver
2 CONT        Radbardsson. That poem is written in Iceland in the twelfth
2 CONT        century, so the poet might not have any better idea of who Audr
2 CONT        was than we do. He even uses the nickname "djupudga"
2 CONT        (deepminded) for her, but that was the nickname of the
2 CONT        Icelandic settler. I don't know who got it from whom.
2 CONT        E-Mail
2 CONT     b. ABT 633
2 CONT     r. Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Radbard of Russia King of Garderidge (Russia) (638-)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: [listed under entry for Radbard of Russia]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Name: Aud IVARSDOTTER  Sex: F  Birth: ABT 633 in Am, Denmark  Death: UNKNOWN
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Ivar HALFDANSSON , King Of Sweden b: ABT 612 in Denmark  Mother: Gauthild ALFSDATTER b: ABT 614 in Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Hraerek HALFDANSSON b: ABT 629 in Am, Denmark Children
2 CONT  Harald HRAEREKSSON b: ABT 655 in Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 2 Radbert Of GARDARIGE , King Of Gardarige b: ABT 638 Children
2 CONT  RANDVER b: ABT 670 in Sweden
2 CONT  RADBERTSDOTTER b: ABT 670 in Sweden
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Noteringar  Aud var först gift med Rurik Sløngvanbug (født ca 640. Konge) Hun ble gift med Kong Radbard I sitt andre ekteskap og levde så i Gårdarike 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
