1 NOTE Kong Halvdan matille / den gavmilde  Sønn av kong Øystein. Arvet riket etter sin far (Vestfold og Romerike). Han fikk ord på seg til å gi hærmennene sine like mange gullpenger i lønn som andre ga sølvpenger, men han sultet dem på 
2 CONC mat. Han var stor hærmann og dro i viking og hentet seg rikdom. Gift med Liv, datter til kong Dag fra Vestmar. Døde på sotteseng på hovedgården sin Holtan i Vestfold og ble hauglagt på Borre. Far til Gudrød Veidekonge.
1 NOTE King in Vestfold.
2 CONT Halvdan døde etter 780, Holtan på Vesterøya i Sandefjord, gravlagt: hauglagt på Borrestranda, konge i Vestfold.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yrke: Halvdan 'Gold Kind' and 'Food Evil', småkung i Vestfold, Norge
2 CONT Far: Eystein (Fart) HALVDANSSON (702 - 755)
2 CONT Mor: Hildur ERIKSDOTTER (710 - 760)
2 CONT
2 CONT Händelse Datum Plats Källa
2 CONT Födelse omkr 750 Norge, Vestfold Tom Björnstad
2 CONT Död omkr 802 Norge, Vestfold, Borre Tom Björnstad
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med Liv DAGSDOTTER (740 - )
2 CONT Barn: Gudröd (Veidekonge) HALVDANSSON (765 - 826)
2 CONT
2 CONT Noteringar
2 CONT Enligt sagorna var Halvdan en vänlig man med sitt guld, men extremt omsorgsfull med sin mat; därför fick han smeknamnet Halvdan 'den milde och matsnåle'. (Källa: Tom Björnstad
2 CONT
2 CONT 887254192. Konge Halfdan Den milde og den madilde ØYSTEINSSØN på Vestfold(22027) died in Holte.(22028) He was a Konge in Vestfold.(22029) Så er sagt at han gav sine menn i lønn likesaa mange gullpenger somandre gav sølvpenger, m
2 CONC en han sultet dem på mat". Hans hovedgård, hvor han bodde og døde, var holte på Vestfold. På langvarig vikingtog, antaglig til Nordtyskland eller egnene der omkring, samlet han sig en stor formue. Han er høilagt på Borrestran
2 CONC den. He was married to Liv DAGSDTR.
1 NOTE Konge i Vestfold. Holtan er hovedgården hans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alias: Halvtan den gjevmilde og matille - Halfdan den milde
1 NOTE Halvdan I Olavsson Hvitbein, 
2 CONT (vers 715 Varmland, Suède - Toten, Uppland, Danemark -)
2 CONT King in Norway Uplanders, of Romerika and Vestfold (685-745),
2 CONT Le premier roi qui a laissé des traces archéologiques.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan was brought up in Soleyar, in the house of his mother's brother Solve, and was called Halfdan Hvitbein. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the people of Vermeland realized that Olaf was not responsible for the people going hungry, so they went across the Eida Forest with all their men and came to Soleyar where Olaf's son, Halfdan, was being raised by King Sol
2 CONC ve. They killed Solve, took Halfdan prisoner, and made him their king. He then subdued Soleyar and Romerike. He later subdued a great part of Hedemark, Toten, Hadeland and Vestfold. Halfdan was king of Romerika and Vestfold while 
2 CONC his brother, Ingjald, was king of Vermeland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those of the Swedes who had more understanding found that the dear times proceeded from there being a greater number of people on the land than it could support, and that the king could not be blamed for this. They took the resolu
2 CONC tion, therefore, to cross the Eida forest with all their men, and came quite unexpectedly into Soleyar, where they put to death King Solve, and took Halfdan Hvitbein prisoner, and made him their chief, and gave him the title of ki
2 CONC ng. Thereupon he subdued Soleyar, and proceeding with his army into Raumarike, plundered there, and laid that district also in subjection by force of arms. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan Hvitbein became a great king. He was married to Aasa, a daughter of Eystein the Severe, who was king of the Upland people, and ruled over Hedemark. Halfdan and Aasa had two sons, Eystein and Gudrod. Halfdan subdued a great
2 CONC  part of Hedemark, Toten, Hadeland, and much of Westfold. He lived to be an old man, and died in his bed at Toten, from whence his body was transported to Westfold, and was buried under a mound at a place called Skaereid, at Skiri
2 CONC ngsale.
