2 CONT Halfdan (Old Norse) or Healfdene (Beowulf) or Haldan (Danish Latin sources) (late 5th century, early 6th century) was a legendary Danish king of the Scylding (Skjöldung) lineage, the son of king named Fróði in many accounts, noted
2 CONC  mainly as the father to the two kings who succeeded him in the rule of Denmark, kings named Hroðgar and Halga in the Old English poem Beowulf and named Hróar and Helgi in Old Norse accounts.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Chronicon Lethrense and Saxo Grammaticus' Gesta Danorum (Book 2), Halfdan had two brothers named Ro and Skat who also sought the throne. Both were killed by Halfdan. Saxo adds that his brothers' supporters were ha
2 CONC nged and that Halfdan continued to reign with great cruelty, but that he reigned long and died peaceably in extreme old age.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga gives Halfdan (in this work also son of a king named Fróði) a brother named Fridleif and says both were great warriors but that Halfdan was the better of the two. This might have been a lead-in to a feud between 
2 CONC the brothers if Snorri had been dealing with Danish matters rather than Swedish matters. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halfdan Wikipedia,en Halfdan]
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorri here only tells us that Halfdan attacked King Aun of Sweden and drove him into exile into Götaland. Halfdan then ruled Sweden for twenty years until he died in Uppsala of sickness and was buried in a mound.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hálfdán fikk sønnene:  1. Hrærekur 'slöngvinbaugi' Hálfdánarson som giftet seg med Aud Ivarsdatter (633) og fikk sønnen Harald 'hildetonn' Hræreksson, f.655, d 735 samt en datter f. 657 2. Helgi 'hvassi' Hálfdánarson 3. Hróar Hálf
2 CONC dánarson 4. samt datteren Signe  en kilde oppgir Halfdan som far til Hroar, og hopper over Helgi og Hroll Krakl??? Halfdan skal også ha fått en sønn med Yrsa Helgaóttir, nemlig Rolf Krake 
