1 NOTE King in Sweden from 623 to 640. After his father’s death, Olaf fled to Vermland. He was married to Solveig, a daughter of Halfdan Guldtand. When famine came to the land, the people burned Olaf’s house with him in it as a sacrifice
2 CONC  to appease the gods. 
1 NOTE Alias/AKA Olaf Ingjallsson "The Woodcutter"
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
2 CONT Original individual @P2203971632@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@) merged with @P2203972602@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@)
1 NOTE Sacrificed his own people in time of famine. The Last Ynglingruler ofUppsala
1 NOTE Olaf the Woodcutter (Tree-Hewer) King of Vermaland in Norway was sacrificed to Woden by his own people during famine according to the sagas about 710.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-2782
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT       1. The Viking Age, Gen. Hst. 19, v. 1, p. 67
2 CONT       2. Attarskra Bjarni Thorsteinsson, Ice FH 1, p. 431
2 CONT       3. Hist. of the Anglo-Saxons, Eng. 36, v. 1, p. 242
2 CONT       4. Keiser und Koenig Hist., Gen. Hist. 25, pt 1, p. 137
