1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gauthild Algautesdotter (Gauthildur Algautesdóttir)
2 CONT
2 CONT (In English: Gauthild daughter of Algaute)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=nor&person=Gauthild%20Algautesdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthild Algautsdottir av Götaland (610 - 640) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthild av GÖTALAND
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthild married Ingjald Illråde Anundsson, son of Anund (Bröt-Anund) Yngvarsson and Unknown. (Ingjald Illråde Anundsson was born about 610.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT (7th century) was according to the Heimskringla, the daughter of the Geatish king Algaut and the wife of Ingjald Ill-ruler, a legendary king of Sweden. She was the mother of Olof Trätälja, the last Yngling ruler of Sweden and Åsa 
2 CONC who married Gudröd, a legendary king of Skåne.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Allmänna hänvisningar: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hennes morfar var Olof den skarpsynt , konungen i Nerike .
2 CONT
2 CONT Från "The Ynglinga Saga " :
2 CONT
2 CONT " 46 . OLAF trädens FELLER .
2 CONT
2 CONT ... Olaf Tree - huggare mor hette Gauthild , och hennes mor var Alov , dotter till Olav den skarpsynt , kung i Nerike . ... "
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthild gifte Ingjald Illråde Anundsson . ( Ingjald Illråde Anundsson föddes omkring 610 . )
2 CONT
2 CONT   Äktenskap Anmärkningar: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Från "The Ynglinga Saga " :
2 CONT
2 CONT " 38 . AV Ingjald de dåliga.
2 CONT
2 CONT ... När Ingjald var vuxen , ansökte Anund för honom till kung Algaut för sin dotter Gauthild . Algaut var son till Gautrek Mild , och sonson till Gaut , och från dem Gotland ( Götland ) tog sitt namn . Kung Algaut trodde att hans 
2 CONC dotter skulle vara väl gift om hon fick kung Anund son , och om han hade sin fars sinnelag , så att flickan skickades till Sverige, och kung Ingjald firade sitt bröllop med henne i tid. "
2 CONT
2 CONT " 43 . DÖDSFALL av kungarna Granmar OCH HJORVARD .
2 CONT
2 CONT ... Kung Ingjald hade två barn med sin hustru - den äldsta heter Aasa , den andra Olaf . Gauthild skickade hustrun till Ingjald , pojken till sin fosterfader Bove , i västra Gotland, där han växte upp tillsammans med Sachsen , Bov
2 CONC e son, som hade efternamnet Flette . ... " 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Källor
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Wikipedia ( http://en.wikipedia.org/ ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Snorre Sturlasson (ca 1179 till 1241 ), http://sunsite.berkeley.edu/OMACL/ ( Om 1225 ) , "Den YNGLINGA Saga " . 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthildr Algautsdóttir (Swedish: Göthild Algottsdotter) (7th century) was, according to the Heimskringla, the daughter of the Geatish king Algaut and the wife of Ingjald Ill-ruler, a legendary king of Sweden. She was the mother o
2 CONC f Olof Trätälja, the last Yngling ruler of Sweden and Åsa who married Gudröd, a legendary king of Skåne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olof Trätälja
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother was Gauthild, a princess of West Götaland, whose maternal grandfather was Olof the Sharp-sighted, the king of Nerike.
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother sent him to his foster-father Bove in West Götaland, where he grew up with his foster-brother Saxe who was surnamed Flette.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Olof heard of his father's death, he assembled the men who were willing to follow him and went to his kinsmen in Nerike, because after his father's atrocities, the Swedes had grown hostile towards the Ynglings.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Swedes learnt that Olof and his kin had sought refuge in Nerike, they were attacked and had to head west through deep and mountainous forests (Kilsbergen) to Lake Vänern and the estuary of Klarälven (where Karlstad is pre
2 CONC sently situated). Here, they settled and cleared land. Soon they had created a whole province called Värmland, where they could make good living.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Swedes learnt that Olof was clearing land, they were amused and called him the Tree-feller. Olof married a woman named Solveig who was a daughter of Halfdan Guldtand of Soleyar. Olof and Solveigh had two sons, Ingjald Olo
2 CONC fsson and Halfdan Hvitbeinn, who were brought up in Soleyar in the house of his mother's uncle Sölve.
2 CONT
2 CONT Because of king Ivar Vidfamne and his harsh rule many Swedes emigrated to Värmland, and they became so numerous that the province could not sustain them. The land was afflicted by famine of which the Swedes accused the king. It wa
2 CONC s an old tradition in Sweden of holding the king responsible for the wealth of the land (see Domalde). The Swedes accused Olof of neglecting his sacrifices to the gods and believed that this was the cause of the famine.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish settlers thus rebelled against Olof, surrounded his house on the shores of lake Vänern and burnt him inside it. Thus he was sacrificed to Odin, like his ancestor Domalde.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
