2 CONT Födelse omkr 620 Västergötland, Sverige Egen beräkning
2 CONT Död Uppland, C Egen beräkning
2 CONT Familj med Ingjald 'Illråde' ANUNDSSON (620 - 655)
2 CONT Barn: Olof (Trätälja) INGJALDSSON (650 - 690)
2 CONT Noteringar
2 CONT När Ingjald blev vuxen fanns hans far, 'Bröt-Anund' Ingvarsson, en lämplig hustru åt honom i Västergötland. Hon hette Göthild och var dotter till kungen där, Algöt. Denne ansåg att det skulle bli ett bra gifte och sände
2 CONC  flickan till Svitjod, där hon firade bröllop med Ingjald. (Källa: Svitjod, Mats G. Larsson)
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
2 CONT Original individual @P2203971637@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@) merged with @P2203972610@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@)
1 NOTE Her maternal grandfather was Olof the Sharp-sighted, the king of Nerike.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The Ynglinga Saga":
2 CONT
2 CONT "46. OF OLAF THE TREE-FELLER.
2 CONT ... Olaf Tree-feller's mother was called Gauthild, and her mother was Alov, daughter of Olaf the Sharp-sighted, king in Nerike. ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The Ynglinga Saga":
2 CONT
2 CONT "38. OF INGJALD THE BAD.
2 CONT ... When Ingjald was grown up, Onund applied for him to King Algaut for his daughter Gauthild. Algaut was a son of Gautrek the Mild, and grandson of Gaut; and from them Gotland (Gautland) took its name. King Algaut thought his dau
2 CONC ghter would be well married if she got King Onund's son, and if he had his father's disposition; so the girl was sent to Sweden, and King Ingjald celebrated his wedding with her in due time."
2 CONT
2 CONT "43. DEATH OF THE KINGS GRANMAR AND HJORVARD.
2 CONT ... King Ingjald had two children by his wife -- the eldest called Aasa, the other Olaf. Gauthild, the wife of Ingjald, sent the boy to his foster-father Bove, in West Gotland, where he was brought up along with Saxe, Bove's son, 
2 CONC who had the surname of Flette. ..."
1 NOTE Källa: http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~jatree/Your%20Ancestor%27s%20Tree/people/p000006u.htm#I508
1 NOTE Olaf mother was called Gauthild, and her mother was Alov, daughter of Olaf the Sharp-sighted, king in Nerike.
2 CONT
