1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.germanicmythology.com/FORNALDARSAGAS/FraFornjotiHardman.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Valdar, legendary Danish king.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Basics ==
2 CONT * Father: Hroar son of Halfdan
2 CONT * Son: Harald the Old
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT The Old Norse genealogy work Hversu Noregr byggdist tells that Hróarr had a son named Valdar, the father of Harald the Old, the father of Halfdan the Valiant, the father of Ivar Vidfamne, who was the maternal grandfather of Harald
2 CONC  Wartooth. Harald fell at the Battle of the Brávellir against his nephew Sigurd Ring, a king of Sweden and the father of Ragnar Lodbrok.
2 CONT
2 CONT Norwegian: "Harald den gamle, sønn av Valdar den gavmilde Hroarsønn, var gift med kong Heidreks datter, Hervor. Sønnen deres var Halfdan den rådkloke, far til Ivar den vidfadme, far til Aud den dyptenkte."
2 CONT
2 CONT Icelandic: "Haraldr inn gamli, sonr Valdars ins milda Hróarssonar, átti Hervöru Heiðreksdóttur konungs. Þeira sonr var Hálfdan snjalli, faðir Ívars víðfaðma, föður Auðar innar djúpauðgu."
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.heimskringla.no/wiki/Hvorledes_Norge_ble_bosatt (in Norwegian)
2 CONT
2 CONT This account is not about presenting the life of Hroðgar, but in presenting how Harald Fairhair was descended from kings and heroes in Scandinavian legend. The only reason for assuming that Hróarr is the same as Hroðgar, the Scyld
2 CONC ing, is the fact that only Hroðgar would be a personage of old so famous so as not to need any further identification than his name. However, the Skjöldunga saga tells that a Valdar disputed that Rörek, the cousin of Halga succeed
2 CONC ed Hroðulf (Hrólfr Kraki) as the king of the Daner. After the war, Rörek took Zealand, while Valdar took Skåne. If based on the same tradition as Hversu Noregr byggdist, Valdar had the right to claim the throne being the son of th
2 CONC e former king Hroðgar.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Link to this version of the Skjoldunga saga needed)
2 CONT == Other stuff ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Valdar Hroarsson (547-) [Pedigree]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Hroar Halfdansson (526-) and Ogne (530-)
2 CONT
2 CONT     b. c. 547, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Hildis Princess of Vandals (-572)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Harold Valdarsson (568-) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. "Royalty for Commoners",
2 CONT          Roderick W. Stuart, 1992, 2nd edition.
2 CONT          This book lists all of the known ancestors of John of Gaunt,
2 CONT          which amounts to most of the Medieval royalty of Europe. Also
2 CONT          see the following article: "A Mediaeval Miscellany:
2 CONT          Commentaries on Roderick W. Stuart's Royalty for Commoners,"
2 CONT          The American Genealogist 69 (April 1994)
2 CONT
2 CONT Valdar Hroarsson born Abt 0547 Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT father:
2 CONT *Hroar Halfdansson born Abt 0526 Roskilde, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT mother:
2 CONT *Ogne Princess of Northumberland born Abt 0530 Northumberland married Abt 0546 Denmark (end of information)
2 CONT
2 CONT siblings: Agner Hroarsson born Abt 0549 Denmark
