1 OCCU King Of Kvenland."Oli kuningas kutsui Fornjotur joka hallitsi Suomessa", Konge, King of Kvenland, king in Kvenland, koning van Kvenland, Norse King of Kvenland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Name: Frosti or Jøkull
2 CONT * Father: Kari Fornjotsson
2 CONT * Son: Snær den Gamle (Snow the Old)
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Kvenland, in modern Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE - another Frosti, father of Skjalf, is also listed on Geni as "king in Finland". Likely not the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT His legend comes out of the "Orkneyinga Saga":
2 CONT
2 CONT Fornjot had three sons;  one was named Hler, whom we call Ægir, the second Logi, the third Kari;  he was the father of Frost, the father of Snow the old" (quoted from http://www.sacred-texts.com/neu/ice/is3/is302.htm)
2 CONT
2 CONT Another version is recorded in the "Flateyjarbok", "Hversum Noregr Byggdist" - here, his name is Jokull, son of Kari, father of Snæ: "Fornjot het en mann og han hadde tre sønner. Den første het Hler, den andre Logi og den tredje K
2 CONC åri. Sistnevnte rådde for vinden, Logi for ilden og Hler for sjøen. Kåri var far til Jøkul, far til kong Snæ"
2 CONT
2 CONT See:
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sn%C3%A6r
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hversu_Noregr_byggdist
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The old, but still popular, LDS gedcom, and gedcoms derived from it, have WRONG information about this person. They list Frosti as father of Jøkul, denoting them as two different persons. There is no known source that suppor
2 CONC ts this speculation.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.celtic-casimir.com/webtree/3/2819.htm Born: Abt 240, Finland Married: Abt 274, Finland
2 CONT
