1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Angantyr Heidreksson konge over Reidgotaland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han var sønn av Heidrek. og Helga, de hadde sønnen Angantyr. Heidreks sønn Angantyr ble utropt til konge i Reidgotaland etter ham, men han svor på at han ikke skulle bestige tronen før faren var blitt hevnet. Han lette så opp de n
2 CONC i trellene og drepte dem. https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heidrek
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/brynjulf?lang=no&pz=tor&nz=langballe&ocz=0&p=angantyr&n=heidreksson
2 CONT
2 CONT Angantyr Heidreksson: Heidrek hadde datteren Hervor og sønnene Angantyr og Hlod. Da goternes konge Heidrek døde overtok Angantyr arven og nektet å gi Hlod sin andel. Hlod angrep med støtte av hunerhæren og i en episk kamp ble Hlod
2 CONC  drept. Legenden om kampen mellom Angantyr og Hlod har klare historiske referanser til kamper mellom gotere og hunere på 300-tallet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Angantyr ble en av forfedrene til den svenske kongeslekten Munsöætten.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muns%C3%B6%C3%A6tten
2 CONT
2 CONT Angantyr was king over Reidgotaland for many years. He was powerful and a great warrior, and from him are descended lines of kings. His son was Heidrek Wolfhide, who succeeded him and ruled long in Reidgotaland. He had a daughter 
2 CONC called Hild. She was the mother of Halfdan Snjalli, father of Ivar the Wide-Grip.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Kung Angantyr Heidreksson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Född: Abt 532 , Reidgotalandi 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Helga Haraldsdatter 
2 CONT
2 CONT Heidrek married Helga Haraldsdatter, daughter of Harald and Unknown. (Helga Haraldsdatter was born about 0512 in , , , Norway 19.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Reidgotaland''', from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reidgotaland Reidgotaland]
2 CONT
2 CONT The oldest regions labelled Reidgotaland (in red and orange). The purple area is the Roman Empire and the pink area is Gotland.  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reidgotaland#/media/File:Chernyakhov.PNG 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Reidgotaland, Reidgothland, Reidgotland, Hreidgotaland or Hreiðgotaland''' was a land in Scandinavian sagas as well as in the pre-Viking English Widsith, which usually referred to the land of the Goths.
2 CONT
2 CONT Etymology and Location
2 CONT
2 CONT Oddly, hreiðr can mean "bird's nest" and perhaps it was a kenning for the Goths tradition of moving and "nesting" in new territories, but hreið- is also a name-prefix meaning "beautiful", "eager", "great", "famous", "noble". Anoth
2 CONC er possibility is that it was originally reið "ride, journey" (see Raidô). The use of the prefix is simple as the same tribal name was used for the Gutes of Gotland. The identification of the territory varies between the sources. 
2 CONC This is the list of meanings given by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nordisk_familjebok Nordisk familjebok]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotland The Island of Gotland].
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%B6taland Götaland].
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. The land of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goths Goths], i.e. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gothiscandza Gothiscandza]  and their later territories. In Hervarar saga, it was the same as Oium and bordered the land of the Hu
2 CONC ns from which it was separated by Myrkviðr.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. The territories of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goths Goths] in southern Europe, according to Anglo-Saxon sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark Denmark] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweden Sweden] (according to Snorri's Edda it was the earthly kingdom of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odin Odin]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark Denmark]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jutland Jutland].
2 CONT
2 CONT The second edition of Nordisk familjebok explains that Hreidgoths was originally applied to the Ostrogoths in south-eastern Europe. It appears as hraiðgutum on the Rök Stone in Östergötland. In Hervarar saga, the name Hreiðgotalan
2 CONC d is applied to the territories of the Ostrogoths in south-eastern Europe. In Widsith, the traveller has been with the Hreðgotum. In Snorri's Edda, it is either applied to Jutland or to Scandinavia as a whole, while the islands ar
2 CONC e called Eygotaland. In the Legendary sagas however, Eygotaland is used only for the island of Gotland in the Baltic Sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reidgotaland Reidgotaland]
