1 NOTE King of Upsal (Sweden), roi de Suède de 460 à 505.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adils Ottarsson, King of Upsal, b. ca. 450 in Sweden, d. 505 in Upsal, Sweden 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Ottar "Vendilkraka" Egilsson, King of Upsal, b. ca. 430 in Sweden, d. 460 in Denmark
2 CONT Spouse: Yrsa Helgasdotter, b. ca. 450 in Denmark, m. Helgi Halfdansson, King of Denmark, ca. 490 
2 CONT         Father: Helgi Halfdansson, King of Denmark
2 CONT         Mother: Alof "the Great"
2 CONT Yrsa was taken prisoner by, and made the wife of, King Helgi of Denmark. She later found out that King Helgi was her own father and her mother was Queen Alof the Great, wife of King Geirthjof of Saxland. Yrsa's son by Helge, Rolf 
2 CONC Krake, later became king of Denmark.
2 CONT Married ca. 470 in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eystein Adilsson, King of Upsal, b. ca. 480 in Sweden, d. 531 in Sweden
