1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''Gudlaug Heimgestsson, King of Hålogaland''''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: Heimgest
2 CONT * Son: Gylaug
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ynglingesagaen" tells from around the year 500 about Gudlaug håløygkonge, who when he was with an army ship in Denmark, was captured and hanged by King Jørund from Uppsala "Jørund and Eirik were the sons of King Yngve Alreksson, 
2 CONC They were out on an army ship all this time and were great army men. One summer they ravaged in Denmark, then they met Gudlaug, king of the Hollow-eyed, and came into conflict with him, and it ended with Gudlaug's ship being clear
2 CONC ed and he himself captured; they put him ashore at Straumøynes, and there they hanged him. His men threw a pile after him there." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Quote: 23. the sons of Yngve Alrekson were called Jårund and Eirik; they were all this time on army ships and were great army men. One summer they ravaged in Denmark and came across Gudlaug, king of the Haaløigs[63]; they held bat
2 CONC tle with him, and the end of it was that Gudlaug's ship was cleared, but he himself was captured; they moved him to land at Strømønes[64] and hanged him there. His men there threw up a heap after him. So says Øivind skalde-spilder
