2 CONC ngs, cursed by his stepmother, according to Snorri Sturluson, with ósgæssa, "ill-luck". He was the son of Visbur <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> In Norse mythology, Domalde, Dómaldi or Dómaldr (Old Norse possibly "Power to J
2 CONC udge"[1]) was a Swedish king of the House of Ynglings, cursed by his stepmother, according to Snorri Sturluson, with ósgæssa, "ill-luck". He was the son of Visbur.
