1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The source for Danp is this line from Ynglingatal, when speaking of the Swedish kings:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Dygve's mother was Drott, a daughter of King Danp, the son of Rig, who was first called "king" in the Danish tongue. His descendants always afterwards considered the title of king the title of highest dignity. Dygve was the first
2 CONC  of his family to be called king, for his predecessors had been called "Drottnar", and their wives "Drottningar", and their court "Drott". Each of their race was called Yngve, or Yngune, and the whole race together Ynglinger. The 
2 CONC Queen Drott was a sister of King Dan Mikillati, from whom Denmark a took its name"
