2 CONT Kung. Son till Sveigder. Bodde troligen på kungsgården i Skuttunge utanför Uppsala. Dödrides av maran. Brändes och höglades vid Skutaån, dvs Björklingeån, inne i nuvarande Lövstalöt. Gift med Driva, dotter till Snjå den gamle (Sna
2 CONC er gamli).
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------- http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanlandi <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> Vanlandi or Vanlande (Old Norse "Man from the Land of the Vanir"[1]) was a Swedish king at Uppsala of the House of Yngling in Norse m
2 CONC ythology. He was the son of Sveigðir whom he succeeded as king. He married a girl from Finnland (territories inhabited by Finno-Ugric peoples), but forgot about her. In revenge, the girl arranged so that Vanlandi was hag ridden to
2 CONC  death. He was succeeded by his son Visbur.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------- 4. VINLANDE or VINLANDI- a Swedish king who married Driva, daughter of Snow the Old from Finland, where he spent one winter. Vinlande left Finland in the spring, promising to return within three years. When he
2 CONC  had not returned after ten years, Driva sent the son she had by Vinlande to his father in Sweden and sought: the help of a witch to either kill Vinlande or force him to rerurn to Finland. During a nightmare, Vinlande was trampled
2 CONC  to death by "Mara" (the nightmare or female ghost). Their son was:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. VISBUR - Swedish King who was killed by his sons from his first wife. <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> BIOGRAFI:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicknames: "Vanlande Sveigdeson Svegdassal", "Vanland", "Vanlandi", "Svegdasson", "Vanlade", "Svegdisson", "Sveigðisson", "Svegdasson of Vanlande", "*Vanlandi /Svegdasson/"
