2 CONC em och hade med henne sonen Vanlande. Sveigder for åter bort för att söka Gudhem. I den östra delen av Svitjod finns en stor gård som heter Stein. Där finns det en sten som är stor som ett hus. På kvällen efter solnedgången när Sv
2 CONC eigder och hans män, mycket druckna, gick från dryckeslaget till sovhuset såg de att det satt en dvärg vid stenen och sprang dit. Dvärgen stod i dörren till stenen och ropade på Sveigder och bad honom komma in om han ville möta Od
2 CONC en. Sveigder sprang in och dörren stängdes efter honom och han kom aldrig ut igen. <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> Svegde etter Sveigde (Sveigdir) var ein mytisk konge av Ynglingeætta, son av Fjolne og far til Vanlande. Han 
2 CONC er omtala i Ynglingesoga og i Den eldste Noregshistoria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre Sturlason fortel at Svegde hadde svore ein eid på at han ville leite etter Godheim og gamle Odin. Difor reiste han ute med tolv mann i fem år, men for så heimatt til Svitjod og ekta ei kvinne frå Vanaheim, som var kalla Van
2 CONC a. Sonen deira var Vanlande. Sidan for Svegde utatt på leit etter Godheim. Ein kveld kom han til ein gard som heitte Stein, der det låg ein stein i tunet, stor som eit hus. Om kvelden var Svegde drukken, og mennene hans med. Då så
2 CONC g dei det sat ein dverg under steinen. Dvergen kalla på Svegde og sa at døra attom var vegen inn til Odin og Godheim. Svegde sprang inn i steinen, og steinen let seg att. Svegde vart aldri meir sett.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ynglingatal fortel:
2 CONT
2 CONT Svegde han sveik, som i svali heldt vakt, den dagrædde for Durins ætt. Inn i steinen den storlynde åsa-frenden flaug etter dvergen, og Sokmimes sal den lysande, av jotunar bygd, vart gjevings grav. Durin og Sokmime er dvergenamn, 
2 CONC som og kan finnast i Dvergatal (ein lut av Voluspå). Dvergen vaktar her døra mellom denne verda og den neste (daudedøra).
2 CONT
2 CONT Den eldste Noregshistoria fortel berre at Svegde følgde dvergen inn i eit berg, og seier beintfram at dette nok lyt takast for eit eventyr. Tilvisinga til Odin er elles tydeleg nok. Odin er og draugedrott (gud for dei daude).
2 CONT
2 CONT Henta frå «http://nn.wikipedia.org/wiki/Svegde»
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------- From Wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sveigðir
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Sveigðir, Sveigder or Swegde (Old Norse "Waving One"[1]) was a Swedish king of the House of Yngling in Norse mythology. He was the son of Fjölner, whom he succeeded as king, and he married Vana of Vanaheimr, probably one of the V
2 CONC anir. Lured by a dwarf, Sveigðir disappeared into a stone and never came back. He was succeeded by his son Vanlandi.' <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> Svegdi took the kingdom after his father, and he made a solemn vow to seek
2 CONC  Godheim and Odin. He went with twelve men through the world, and came to Turkland, and the Great Svithiod, where he
2 CONT
2 CONT found many of his connections. He was five years on this journey; and when he returned home to Sweden he remained there for some time.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had got a wife in Vanheim, who was called Vana, and their son was Vanlande. Svegdi went out afterwards to seek again for Godheim, and came to a mansion on the east side of Swithiod called Stein, where there was a stone as big a
2 CONC s a large house. In the evening after sunset, as Svegdi was going from the drinking-table to his sleeping-room, he cast his eye upon the stone, and saw that a dwarf was sitting under it. Svegdi and his man were very drunk, and the
2 CONC y ran towards the stone. The dwarf stood in the door, and called to Svegdi, and told him to come in, and he should see Odin. Svegdi ran into the stone, which instantly closed behind him, and Swegdi never came back.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thiodolf of Kvine tells of this: --
2 CONT
2 CONT "By Diurnir's elfin race,
2 CONT
2 CONT Who haunt the cliffs and shun day's face,
2 CONT
2 CONT The valiant Swegde was deceived,
2 CONT
2 CONT The elf's false words the king believed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The dauntless hero rushing on,
2 CONT
2 CONT Passed through the yawning mouth of stone:
2 CONT
2 CONT It yawned -- it shut -- the hero fell,
2 CONT
2 CONT In Saekmime's hall, where giants dwell."
2 CONT
2 CONT The Saga tells of his strange demise, also in a state of drunken-ness like his father. One night when Svegde and his men had been drinking excessively and were about to retire for the night, Svegde looked out and saw a large stone
2 CONC  with a dwarf sitting under it. He rushed to the stone where the dwarf opened a door and urged Svegde to enter in order that he could see Odin. Svegde went in and never came out
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------- Notes for Sveigde Fjolnfarssen
2 CONT
2 CONT Reiste i fem år kom bl a til Tyrkland og Store Svitjod.
2 CONT
2 CONT Svegder havde gjort det Løfte at besøge Asernes Stamland ved det sorte Hav, men omkom paa sin niende reise. Sagaen beretter at en Dverg lokkede ham i Bjerg, under Foregivende at han der kulde træffe Othin, hvorefter Bjerget lukked
2 CONC e sig efter ham. <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Some dwarfs lured him into a cave and shut the opening with a huge boulder and he was never seen again. May have been mythical. Disappeared during a journey which he made in order to find Odin the Old. [WBH - Sweden]
2 CONT
2 CONT !Ran after a dwarf when drunk and vanished into a boulder. [A History of the Vikings, p. 37] Son of Fiolner; disappeared during a journey which he made in order to find Odin the old. Father of Vanlande. [History of Sweden, p. 35] 
2 CONC -------------------- Svegdi Fjolnarsson
2 CONT
