2 CONT The Anderson-Krogh genealogy: ancestral lines and descendants
2 CONT Svegdir took the realm after his father, Fjaelnir; he made a vow to search for Godheim and Odin the old. He traveled with twelve men far and wide about the world; he came to Tyrkland and to greater Svitjod and met many of his frie
2 CONC nds and kinsmen. He was gone five years on this journey. Then he came back to Uppsalir and stayed at home for some time. He married a woman called Vana in Vansheim; their son was Vanlande. Svegdir went again in search of Godheim. 
2 CONC In the eastern part of Sweden there is a large estate called Stein; there is a rock there as large as as a big house. One evening after sunset, when Svegdir ceased drinking and went to his sleeping quarters, he saw a dverg (dwarf)
2 CONC  sitting outside the rock. Svegdir and his men were very drunk and ran to the rock. The dverg stood in the door and shouted Svegdir to come in if he wanted to meet Odin. Svegdir rushed into the rock, which at once closed upon him,
2 CONC  and he never came back.
2 CONT
