2 CONT Sveigðir, Sveigder or Swegde was a Swedish king of the House of Yngling in Norse mythology. He was the son of Fjölner, whom he succeeded as king, and he married Vana of Vanaheim, probably one of the Vanir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lured by a dwarf, Sveigðir disappeared into a stone and never came back. He was succeeded by his son Vanlandi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vana also means Vanha in finno-ugric languages as finnish and estonian. Those areas were probably (as still are) having Kvenland/Finland names, that would be the easiest to think about. Also Vanaheim = vanha heimo, means old tribe
2 CONC . Jokkmukk, these are all finnish names in Northern Sweden and Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
