2 CONT
2 CONT Konge i Uppsala (Sverige)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Fjolne Yngvi-Freysson
2 CONT
2 CONT Dødrukken, skulle finne et sted å sove, mistet fotfestet og falt i mjødkaret og druknet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fjølner, Yngve Freys Søn, forstod at vedligeholde samme Fred og Lykke. Paa et Besøg hos den danske Konge Frode Fredgode omkom han ved at falde nedgjennem en Aabning i Gulvet i et Mjødkar, der var stort nok til at lade den berusede
2 CONC  Konge drukne deri.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 14. OF KING FJOLNE'S DEATH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fjolne, Yngve Frey's son, ruled thereafter over the Swedes and
2 CONT
2 CONT the Upsal domains. He was powerful, and lucky in seasons and in
2 CONT
2 CONT holding the peace. Fredfrode ruled then in Leidre, and between
2 CONT
2 CONT them there was great friendship and visiting. Once when Fjolne
2 CONT
2 CONT went to Frode in Sealand, a great feast was prepared for him, and
2 CONT
2 CONT invitations to it were sent all over the country. Frode had a
2 CONT
2 CONT large house, in which there was a great vessel many ells high,
2 CONT
2 CONT and put together of great pieces of timber; and this vessel stood
2 CONT
2 CONT in a lower room. Above it was a loft, in the floor of which was
2 CONT
2 CONT an opening through which liquor was poured into this vessel. The
2 CONT
2 CONT vessel was full of mead, which was excessively strong. In the
2 CONT
2 CONT evening Fjolne, with his attendants, was taken into the adjoining
2 CONT
2 CONT loft to sleep. In the night he went out to the gallery to seek a
2 CONT
2 CONT certain place, and he was very sleepy and exceedingly drunk. As
2 CONT
2 CONT he came back to his room he went along the gallery to the door of
2 CONT
2 CONT another left, went into it, and his foot slipping, he fell into
2 CONT
2 CONT the vessel of mead and was drowned. So says Thjodolf of Kvine:
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT "In Frode's hall the fearful word,
2 CONT
2 CONT The death-foreboding sound was heard:
2 CONT
2 CONT The cry of fey denouncing doom,
2 CONT
2 CONT Was heard at night in Frode's home.
2 CONT
2 CONT And when brave Frode came, he found
2 CONT
2 CONT Swithiod's dark chief, Fjolne, drowned.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Frode's mansion drowned was he,
2 CONT
2 CONT Drowned in a waveless, windless sea."
2 CONT
