2 CONT Legendary Swedish king, King Fjolnir rose in the night to make water, fell into a vat of mead and drowned instead. [A History of the Vikings, p. 37] Son of Yngve; drowned by accident in a huge vessel full of mead during a visit pa
2 CONC ide to King Frode in Denmark; father of Sveigder. [History of Sweden, p. 35] -------------------- Other sources say he was born 32 BC, died in 14 by drowning in a 'mjødkar' during a celebration."In the evening Fjolne, with his att
