0 @N6000000002187965836@ NOTE !Said to have ruled Sweden, Denmark, Saxonland, all of Austria and 1/5 of England. One account has it that Ivar was the head of a new dynastey in Sweden. As he was originally king of Scania, perhaps these were the real Ynglings. [
1 CONC WBH - Sweden]
1 CONT
1 CONT FOSTER, MINOR, NEWLIN LINES
1 CONT
1 CONT !King of Skane when Ingjald the Wicked (of the Yngling line) was king of the Swedes at Uppsala. Ingjald had widened his kingdom by slaying 12 kings, all of them treacherously. Confronted with the wrath of Ivar he withdrew into his
1 CONC  hall with his daughter and people, and when the company was dead drunk he had fire laid to it, so that they all perished. According to Ynglinga Saga, this
1 CONT pyromanic imbecility cost the Ynglings their realm of Uppsala, and future kings of Sweden and Denmark came of the line of Ivar, though what Ivar could be except another Yngling is hard to say. We hear that he now conquered Sweden 
1 CONC and came to possess all Denmark. Also he won for himself a large part of Germany, the entire Austrriki (presumably the lands east of the Baltic, including a little of Russia), and the fifth part of England -- a traditional descrip
1 CONC tion of Northumbria. This source doubts the authenticity of these claims. [A History of the Vikings, p. 52]
1 CONT
1 CONT !Also known as Ivar Wide-Grasper. [A History of the Vikings, p. 147]
1 CONT
1 CONT Lived in the 7th century. Ivar's grandson was Harald Hilditonn or Wartooth. [A History of the Vikings, p. 52]
1 CONT
1 CONT b.c. 612, Denmark; father of Aud who m. Radbard, King of Garderige-Russia. [GRS CD#100]
1 CONT
1 CONT A Skioldung of Skane; King of Uppsala in Sweden and Lethra in Denmark; father of Aud who m.1 Rurick/Hroerekr and m.2 Radbard. [Royalty for Commoners, p. 73]
1 CONT
1 CONT King of Sweden; father of Aud who m. Radbart, king of Garderige-Russia. [WFT Vol 5 Ped 3568]
1 CONT
1 CONT Father of Rurick, grandchild of Rurick. [Royalty for Commoners, p. 73]
1 CONT
1 CONT Son of Halfdan; father of Roric Slingeband. [A.H. Burgess]
1 CONT
1 CONT Son of Halfdan Haroldsson and Maolda 'Digri' Kinriksdatter; m. Gauthild (Gyrithe) Alfsdatter; father of Aud who m. Rurick (Hroerekr) of Lethra, Hraerek 'Slaunvanbauga' Halfdansson and Radbard Skirtasson. [Gary Lewis
1 CONT  Sources:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Repository:
1 CONT             Name: Cheryl Varner Library
1 CONT       Title: World's Best Histories: Sweden
1 CONT       Author: Nilsson, Victor, Ph.D.
1 CONT       Publication: The Co-operative Publication Society, New York and London, 1899
1 CONT    2. Repository:
1 CONT             Name: Cheryl Varner Library
1 CONT       Title: A History of the Vikings
1 CONT       Author: Jones, Gwyn
1 CONT       Publication: Oxford University Press, New York and Toronto, 1968
1 CONT       Page: pp. 52, 147
1 CONT    3. Repository:
1 CONT             Name: Cheryl Varner Library
1 CONT       Title: Royalty for Commoners, Revised Second Edition
1 CONT       Author: Stuart, Roderick W.
1 CONT       Publication: Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., Baltimore, 1995
