0 @N6000000002187913682@ NOTE King of Nerike
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT
1 CONT The Norse sagas relate of a number of kings of Nerike who ruled during the mythological past of Scandinavia.
1 CONT
1 CONT They were:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Nidud from Völundarkviða.
1 CONT     * Olof the Sharp-sighted (Óláfr inn skyggni) whose grand-daughter married Ingjald ill-ruler of the House of Yngling according to the Heimskringla. According to Gautreks saga and Upplendinga Konungum, he aided the Norwegian kin
1 CONC g Vikar in a war together with Starkad.
1 CONT     * Sporsnjall, a form of Fornsnjallr, (in Heimskringla) who was invited by Ingjald to a banquet only to be burnt to death inside Ingjald's hall with a number of other petty kings. Sporsjall appears as Sporsnäll in later legends
1 CONC  from Närke.
