0 @N6000000002322273384@ NOTE ODIN DIVIDES HIS KINGDOM: ALSO CONCERNING GEFION.
1 CONT
1 CONT There goes a great mountain barrier from north-east to south-
1 CONT west, which divides the Greater Swithiod from other kingdoms.
1 CONT South of this mountain ridge it is not far to Turkland, where
1 CONT Odin had great possessions.  In those times the Roman chiefs went
1 CONT wide around in the world, subduing to themselves all people; and
1 CONT on this account many chiefs fled from their domains.  But Odin
1 CONT having foreknowledge, and magic-sight, knew that his posterity
1 CONT would come to settle and dwell in the northern half of the world.
1 CONT He therefore set his brothers Ve and Vilje over Asgaard; and he
1 CONT himself, with all the gods and a great many other people,
1 CONT wandered out, first westward to Gardarike, and then south to
1 CONT Saxland.  He had many sons; and after having subdued an extensive
1 CONT kingdom in Saxland, he set his sons to rule the country.  He
1 CONT himself went northwards to the sea, and took up his abode in an
1 CONT island which is called Odins in Fyen.  Then he sent Gefion across
1 CONT the sound to the north to discover new countries; and she came to
1 CONT King Gylve, who gave her a ploughgate of land.  Then she went to
1 CONT Jotunheim, and bore four sons to a giant, and transformed them
1 CONT into a yoke of oxen.  She yoked them to a plough, and broke out
1 CONT the land into the ocean right opposite to Odins.  This land was
1 CONT called Sealand, and there she afterwards settled and dwelt.
1 CONT Skjold, a son of Odin, married her, and they dwelt at Leidre.
1 CONT Where the ploughed land was is a lake or sea called Laage.  In
1 CONT the Swedish land the fjords of Laage correspond to the nesses in
1 CONT Sealand.  Brage the Old sings thus of it: --
1 CONT
1 CONT      "Gefion from Gylve drove away,
1 CONT      To add new land to Denmark's sway --
1 CONT      Blythe Gefion ploughing in the smoke
1 CONT      That steamed up from her oxen-yoke:
1 CONT      Four heads, eight forehead stars had they,
1 CONT      Bright gleaming, as she ploughed away;
1 CONT      Dragging new lands from the deep main
1 CONT      To join them to the sweet isle's plain.
