0 @N6000000003796269405@ NOTE The Yngling Saga of Heimskingla
1 CONT The Saga of the Norse Kings by Snorri Sturleson
1 CONT (dates may be off):
1 CONT
1 CONT 5. VISBUR - Swedish King who was killed by his sons from his first wife. After Visbur sent away his first wife and two sons in order to take another wife, the first wife sent the two sons back to Visbur to ask him to return their 
1 CONC mother's dowry - three large farms and a gold ornament. Visbur refused to return anything to them. During the night they gathered a group of men and went to Visbur's house where they burned the house with Visbur in it. His son was
1 CONC :
1 CONT
1 CONT 6. DOMALDE 
0 @N6000000002187696074@ NOTE Visbur
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT In Scandinavian mythology, Visbur was a king of the House of Ynglings and the son of Vanlade.
1 CONT
1 CONT Snorri Sturluson relates in Ynglinga saga that Visbur was the son of Vanlade and Drífa, a daughter of Snær the Old. He married a daughter of Aud the Rich, and they had two sons, Gisl and Öndur.
1 CONT
1 CONT However, Visbur found a new wife whereupon his old wife took the two boys and returned to her father.
1 CONT
1 CONT Visbur had a third son, Domalde, by the new wife. When Gisl and Öndur were twelve and thirteen years old they went to their father to retrieve their mothers dowry. Visbur, however, refused to consent, and then the two sons said th
1 CONC at the golden necklace would be the bane of the best man of his house. They then returned and planned to murder their father.
1 CONT
1 CONT The völva Huld was hired to help them, but she prophesied that killing kin would lead to having kinslaying as a permanent trait in the House of Yngling (Scylfing). They did not care about this warning, went to their father and bur
1 CONC nt him to death inside his hall.
1 CONT
1 CONT Snorri included a piece from Ynglingatal in his account in the Heimskringla:
1 CONT
1 CONT     Ok Visburs
1 CONT     vilja byrgi
1 CONT     sævar niðr
1 CONT     svelga knátti,
1 CONT     þá er meinþjóf
1 CONT     markar öttu
1 CONT     setrs verjendr
1 CONT     á sinn föður;
1 CONT     ok allvald
1 CONT     í arinkjóli
1 CONT     glóða garmr
1 CONT     glymjandi beit.[1]
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT     Have the fire-dogs' fierce tongues yelling
1 CONT     Lapt Visbur's blood on his own hearth?
1 CONT     Have the flames consumed the dwelling
1 CONT     Of the here's soul on earth?
1 CONT     Madly ye acted, who set free
1 CONT     The forest foe, red fire, night thief,
1 CONT     Fell brother of the raging sea,
1 CONT     Against your father and your chief.(Laing's translation [2])
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Vanlade Mythological king of Sweden Succeeded by:
1 CONT Domalde
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
